lay outside."},{"text":"nobody did."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-017","slides":[{"text":"some of these tapes sat in a closet for twenty years"},{"text":"waiting for someone to invent youtube."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-018","slides":[{"text":"the blue screen between programs"},{"text":"where the vcr was paused"},{"text":"and then unpaused"},{"text":"two seconds too late."},{"text":"every single tape."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-019","slides":[{"text":"there's a moment on every tape"},{"text":"where someone walks in front of the tv."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-020","slides":[{"text":"you can date a tape by the cereal commercials."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-021","slides":[{"text":"the 1-800 number in the commercial"},{"text":"still works."},{"text":"it's a dentist's office now."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-022","slides":[{"text":"in 1997 abc replaced its cartoon block"},{"text":"with a show about nutrition hosted by a purple blob."},{"text":"viewership dropped ninety percent."},{"text":"they kept it for five years."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-023","slides":[{"text":"the audio warps in the same spot every time."},{"text":"someone paused here."},{"text":"probably to pour more cereal."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-024","slides":[{"text":"these tapes were never meant to be archives."},{"text":"they were meant to be taped over next week."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-025","slides":[{"text":"every toy commercial had the same disclaimer."},{"text":"\"each sold separately.\""},{"text":"each was nine dollars."},{"text":"there were forty of them."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-026","slides":[{"text":"the antenna got three channels."},{"text":"all three had cartoons."},{"text":"monopoly was impossible. abundance was guaranteed."},{"text":"saturday morning."}]},{"id":"sm-027","slides":[{"text":"the local station ran its own bumpers"},{"tex